WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.740
The very beginning of The Nun teaser says
MAKE SURE YOU WATCH TO THE END, in big bold

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.740
caps, I don’t know if that’s just for
YouTube, but there’s nothing at the end

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.740
of this teaser.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:09.740
It just shows the release date.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.150
Then it ends!

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.620
So I don’t know why it says that.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:20.300
But anyways, make sure you watch this Things
You Missed video all the way to the end.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.499
Another year, another installment in the The
Conjuring universe.

00:00:23.499 --> 00:00:27.359
This time it focuses on the Nun demon Valak,
who has been teased at one point or another

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:29.869
in all four Conjuring films so far.

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:33.370
The opening shot of the teaser shows this
painting, it looks a lot like what West Dakota

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.940
looks like when he first wakes up in the morning.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.571
But this is actually the painting that Ed
Warren paints, based off of his dream in The

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.610
Conjuring 2.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.040
That’s the movie where the Warrens have
their big showdown with Valak, but The Nun

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.180
is a prequel, so this is going to be taking
place way before the Warrens are even in the

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.180
picture.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.280
I’ll get back to the overall timeline of
events later in this video.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.900
But the reason it shows this painting relates
to the voiceover.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.900
Roll it.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:01:01.540
“I had a series of visions when I was younger,
and after each one ended, the same thought

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.540
would be stuck in my head.”

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.540
“What did you see?”

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.140
“I saw a Nun.”

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.770
Let’s pause it there.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.409
So this girl has visions of the Nun, just
as Lorraine Warren did in The Conjuring 2,

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:13.040
and Ed Warren did in his dream.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.320
So right away I would make the guess that
she’s a medium.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.119
Then I saw who was speaking these words.

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:22.350
This is an actress named Taissa Farmiga, the
sister of Vera Farmiga, who plays Lorraine

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.360
Warren in The Conjuring films.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.069
We may only be three shots into the teaser,
but I’ve already got a theory: I think this

00:01:28.069 --> 00:01:30.490
girl is somehow related to Lorraine Warren.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.450
This girl does look to be on the younger side,
and with this being a prequel set in 1952

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.909
that would make this girl and Lorraine right
around the same age.

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:40.840
They probably aren’t sisters, seeing as
how The Nun takes place in Romania, and Lorraine

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.450
was born in Connecticut, but they probably
share some common ancestor who passed down

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.929
the medium ability to both of them.

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:49.689
If you’re wondering how I know what year
this place in, I noticed that this shot in

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:54.590
the teaser is the same location as the post-credit
sequence from Annabelle: Creation, where this

00:01:54.590 --> 00:02:13.310
happens.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:17.260
So as promised, quick rundown of the timeline,
the earliest known event is the creation of

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.890
the Annabelle doll in Annabelle: Creation.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.890
Which I guess it why it’s called that.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:25.590
Then in 1943, the car accident from Annabelle:
Creation takes place.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.430
The Nun takes place 9 years later in 1952.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:32.710
Three years after that in 1955 is the rest
of Annabelle creation, which leads right into

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.770
Annebelle’s adoption.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:38.580
Twelve years later in 1967, Annabelle returns
to kill her adoptive parents, beginning the

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.550
events of Annabelle. 1971 is The Conjuring.
1976 is The Conjuring 2.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.560
I bring up the timeline because the history
of Valak is unique in that it stretches at

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.180
least 24 years across three different countries.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.470
It almost makes me wonder if there’s something
that happens in The Nun, that puts a curse

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.900
on the family, and sends Valak to try to kill
Ed and Lorraine?

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.600
So moving on with the teaser, as this creepy
old voice is telling about the abbey’s long

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.340
history, we’re shown this little card.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.410
If you mirror it, it says The Nun at the bottom
there, and the eyes and mouth are crossed

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.410
out in ink.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.450
The overall shape of this image resembles
a stain glass window, so it kind of makes

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.490
me think that The Nun deity was once an agent
of good before being possessed by the evil

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.570
demon Valak.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:19.720
And that idea kind of fits in with this next
shot, a door with the words Finit hic, Deo

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.720
burned into it.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.840
That’s a Latin phrase translating to “This
ends a God”, or as the priest puts it and

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.350
I had to use the subtitles to understand what
he was saying, “God ends here.”

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:32.080
So whatever is behind this door has gotta
be akin to many of the other haunted locations

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.160
in the series.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.000
I wonder if whoever designed this logo was
a Nine Inch Nails fan.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.710
But anyway, that’s it for this teaser.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:41.000
I’ll be sure to come back with more Things
You Missed when we get a full trailer, and

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.950
of course when we get the full movie this
September.

